}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Proof irrelevance.} \code{\verb~|Conv.pirr~} itself is 0.12 \% (0.18 s). What it triggers - \code{\verb~|VTYPE~} of both sides, \code{\verb~|ISPROP~}, the comparison of the two types - is on the stack of 27.5 \% of the samples: 40.8 s of CPU, 5.1 s of wall clock, 41 \% of it hash consing. The ablation agrees: with \code{\verb~|congruence,skipargs~} the same line is 1.4 \% (1.5 s) and the workers need 43.1 s less (section 4).}
\li{\strong{The K rule}: 0.22 \% (0.33 s) inclusive. \strong{Structure eta}: 0.98 \% in conversion (with unit-like types), 0.07 \% as eta of a major premise. \strong{Lambda eta}: 1.0 \%. None of them is where the time goes.}
\li{\strong{Delta and code blocks}: 17.2 \% of the samples are under an unfolding, 15.0 \% under a running code block, and 42 \% of the latter is hash consing: a code block's work is building values.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{2.4 The reference-engine fallback and the term-level store}

\table{
\tr{\th{inside \code{\verb~|ref~} (12.52 \% of the worker samples, 18.56 s CPU), by innermost frame}\th{share of it}\th{CPU s}}
\tr{\td{store.subst}\td{57.7 \%}\td{10.72}}
\tr{\td{ref}\td{21.5 \%}\td{3.99}}
\tr{\td{store.read}\td{16.7 \%}\td{3.10}}
\tr{\td{level}\td{2.2 \%}\td{0.42}}
\tr{\td{store.decls}\td{1.5 \%}\td{0.27}}
}

\ul{
\li{The fallback is the re-check, by the reference kernel, of the units the machine declines: 6,799 of 721,845 (statistics of the same jar: 6,711 at eager reduction, 88 at other limits; the machine tries each of them twice before it gives up - 13,598 declines - and that work is in the machine's lines). It is 12.5 \% of the workers' CPU for 0.94 \% of the units; the reference kernel makes 69.9 M steps in them.}
\li{\strong{Who calls \code{\verb~|TermOps~} / \code{\verb~|Overlay~} (term-level substitution, the overlay's own hash consing of terms)?} On a worker: the reference kernel (\code{\verb~|RefKernel.instRev~} 60 \%, \code{\verb~|mkApps~} 9 \%, \code{\verb~|copy~} 8 \%) and the decoder of proof blocks (20 \%). The machine never does (0.00 \% outside those two contexts). On the environment thread: admission (inductive blocks), through the reference kernel.}
}

\table{
\tr{\th{inside \code{\verb~|store.blocks~} (2.90 \% of the worker samples, 4.31 s CPU), by innermost frame}\th{share of it}\th{CPU s}}
