\ul{
\li{\strong{Interpreter / C1}: 99.999 \% of the samples of the profiled pass are in compiled frames; 0.35 \% in methods that have no C2 code by then (the constructors of the level stores, which run once per worker context; \code{\verb~|Machine.copyOrNull~}, \code{\verb~|Overlay.grow~}). Nothing hot is left below C2 (J1's finding, now with a number).}
\li{\strong{JIT compiler threads}: 2.03 s of CPU in pass 2 (179 C2 tasks for rlvm methods), 0.13 s in pass 3 (22), with \code{\verb~|CICompilerCount=2~}. That is 0.25 s of wall clock in pass 2 and nothing afterwards.}
\li{\strong{Deoptimisation}: 2 events in the profiled pass, 32 rlvm nmethods made not entrant in pass 3.}
\li{\strong{Safepoints}: 27 in the pass, 26 of them collections; 0.62 s in all, of which 3 ms are spent reaching the safepoint. No other VM operation stops the workers.}
\li{\strong{Kernel}: 0.44 s of the process's 164 s (the workers 0.04 s, 407 page faults): the heap is committed and touched once (\code{\verb~|-Xms13g~}).}
}
}

