}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Mathlib: 21.93 -> 19.31 s (-12 \%), process CPU 164.1 -> 148.2 s}; pass 3 of that process 19.80 s; the first (cold) pass 22.5 s instead of 33.4 s. The workers need 13.6 s less CPU (-9 \%), and they save it in the memory-bound lines: universe levels -2.3 s (-20 \%), memo lookups -3.0 s (-18 \%), term store -2.4 s (-14 \%), hash consing -4.5 s (-11 \%); evaluation, conversion and the fallback are unchanged (within 1 s). That is what transparent huge pages buy (fewer TLB walks: the image's hardware events put 17 \% of all data TLB walks into the level stores). JIT threads: 1.09 s in pass 2 with 105 C2 tasks for rlvm methods (shipped line: 2.03 s, 179).}
\li{\strong{The 7 GB heap has a price inside the pass}: 3 of its 27 collections are full collections that the program asks for itself (\code{\verb~|Machine.heapAllows~} calls \code{\verb~|System.gc()~} when a session array does not seem to fit: J1's finding J1-F1), 0.16 s of the 0.52 s of pauses. With the shipped 13 GB there is none.}
\li{\strong{cedar: 1.63 -> 1.53 s}, steady from pass 3 on instead of pass 5 (first pass 4.37 s instead of 6.09 s); JIT CPU in the timed pass 0.11 s instead of 0.71 s.}
\li{The item SHARES do not move by more than 1.5 points (Mathlib, J1's line: hash consing 27.1 \%, memo lookups 10.3 \%, term store 10.8 \%, evaluation and code 17.4 \%, conversion 5.2 \%, inference 7.8 \% + levels 6.9 \%, the fallback 13.7 \%): the table of section 0 holds for both launcher lines.}
}
}
}

